The black-and-tan coonhound's size and proportions are balanced, with a deep chest and strong legs. They have a friendly and gentle temperament, making them excellent family pets. Their unique identifying traits include their keen sense of smell, which they use to track and hunt raccoons and other game animals. They are also known for their loud, distinctive howl, which can be heard for miles. Overall, the black-and-tan coonhound is a versatile and adaptable breed, excelling in both hunting and companionship roles.
