MLLM description: Golden Retrievers are characterized by their distinctive physical features, including a broad head, slightly arched back, and a sturdy build. Their coat is typically a rich golden color, though variations can include cream or light brown shades. The fur is dense, water-repellent, and wavy to medium-length, often with a slightly longer mane around the neck. Their eyes are expressive and almond-shaped, usually dark in color, and their ears are floppy and hang down close to the head.

In terms of size and proportions, Golden Retrievers are medium to large-sized dogs, with males generally weighing between 65-80 pounds and females between 55-70 pounds. They have a muscular yet elegant body structure, with a deep chest and a strong, well-muscled hindquarters.

Behaviorally, Golden Retrievers are known for their friendly, gentle, and affectionate nature. They are highly intelligent, trainable, and make excellent family pets. They are also highly energetic and require regular exercise to maintain their health and happiness.

Unique identifying traits of Golden Retrievers include their distinctive facial features, such as their broad head, slightly arched back, and floppy ears. Additionally, their friendly and outgoing demeanor makes them easily recognizable among other dog breeds.
